/*
class Node {
    int data;
    Node next;

    Node(int x) {
        data = x;
        next = null;
    }
}
*/

class Solution {
    
    Node recursiveReverseList(Node curr, Node prev) {     // Helper function for tail-recursive reversal
        
        if (curr == null) { return prev; }              // Base case: end of list
        
        Node next = curr.next;                          // Save next node
        curr.next = prev;                               // Reverse current link
        
        return recursiveReverseList(next, curr);        // Recurse with moved pointers
    }
    
    // Main function (call this)
    Node reverseList(Node head) {
        return recursiveReverseList(head, null);        // Start with prev = null
    }
}

//////////////////////// DRY RUN /////////////////////////////

Input: 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 -> null

ORIGINAL LIST (Before Recursion):

[1|•] -> [2|•] -> [3|•] -> [4|•] -> null
 ^
curr
prev = null


RECURSION CALLS (Going Down - Reversing as We Go):

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Call 1: recursiveReverseList(curr=1, prev=null)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        next = curr.next = 2
        curr.next = prev  →  1.next = null
        
        [1|•]    [2|•] -> [3|•] -> [4|•] -> null
         ^        ^
       prev     next
       curr
        
        Returns: recursiveReverseList(2, 1)


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Call 2: recursiveReverseList(curr=2, prev=1)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        next = curr.next = 3
        curr.next = prev  →  2.next = 1
        
        null <- [1|•] <- [2|•]    [3|•] -> [4|•] -> null
                 ^        ^        ^
               prev    curr      next
        
        Returns: recursiveReverseList(3, 2)


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Call 3: recursiveReverseList(curr=3, prev=2)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        next = curr.next = 4
        curr.next = prev  →  3.next = 2
        
        null <- [1|•] <- [2|•] <- [3|•]    [4|•] -> null
                          ^        ^       ^
                        prev    curr     next
        
        Returns: recursiveReverseList(4, 3)


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Call 4: recursiveReverseList(curr=4, prev=3)  [LAST NODE]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        next = curr.next = null
        curr.next = prev  →  4.next = 3
        
        null <- [1|•] <- [2|•] <- [3|•] <- [4|•]    null
                                   ^        ^       ^
                                 prev    curr     next
        
        Returns: recursiveReverseList(null, 4)


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Call 5: recursiveReverseList(curr=null, prev=4)  [BASE CASE]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        curr == null → return prev (which is 4)
        
        Returns: 4 (NEW HEAD)


FINAL REVERSED LIST:

null <- [1|•] <- [2|•] <- [3|•] <- [4|•]
                                 ^
                              prev (NEW HEAD)


Output: 4 -> 3 -> 2 -> 1 -> null


SUMMARY TABLE:

Call    curr    prev    next    Action              Next Call
----    ----    ----    ----    ------              ---------
1       1       null    2       1.next = null       recursiveReverseList(2, 1)
2       2       1       3       2.next = 1          recursiveReverseList(3, 2)
3       3       2       4       3.next = 2          recursiveReverseList(4, 3)
4       4       3       null    4.next = 3          recursiveReverseList(null, 4)
5       null    4       -       Return prev (4)     DONE


KEY DIFFERENCE FROM PREVIOUS APPROACH:

• Previous (Head Recursion): Reverse happens while UNWINDING (coming back)
• This (Tail Recursion): Reverse happens while GOING DOWN (before recursive call)

Space Complexity: O(n) - recursion stack
Time Complexity: O(n) - single pass


